.TH GENESIS-RETINA 1 "November 2026" "Genesis 0.2.0" "Genesis Manual"
.SH NAME
genesis-retina \- the eye: sole V4L2 capture process for Genesis
.SH SYNOPSIS
Launched automatically by
.BR genesis-cli (1)
before the daemon; not normally invoked by hand.
.PP
.B genesis-retina
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B genesis-retina
is the only process that ever opens the camera. It opens the V4L2
device named by
.B GENESIS_CAMERA
(default
.IR /dev/video0 ),
requests 640x480 RGB24 (falling back to YUYV), and publishes raw
frames into the POSIX shared-memory segment
.IR /genesis_optic_nerve
\(em the optic nerve \(em which the daemon and the mind read but
never write.
.PP
The daemon carries no capture limb of its own: if no retina is
running, or the retina dies, the organism is blind until it returns.
The retina is therefore the eye's only connection, and exactly one
process can own the camera at a time.
.PP
An absent or dying camera is re-opened on a bounded backoff table
and then accepted absent \(em sight is a degradation, never a fault.
On SIGINT/SIGTERM the limb winds down and the segment's name is
unlinked, so a dead eye never publishes stale frames under a live
name.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GENESIS_CAMERA
Linux V4L2 capture device. Default
.IR /dev/video0 .
.TP
.B GENESIS_DATA_DIR
Data-directory binding used by the CLI to identify and adopt the
process.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /genesis_optic_nerve
Canonical frame mapping (POSIX shared memory); this process is its
sole publisher.
.TP
.I $DATA_DIR/retina.log
Capture diagnostics.
.TP
.I $DATA_DIR/genesis_retina.pid
PID file written by the supervising CLI.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR genesis (1),
.BR genesis-cli (1),
.BR genesis-daemon (8),
.BR genesis-vision (7)
